00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.600
Tells us how many claims the company has

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.600
And how many claims it has passed So this should be more

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.600
But along with this

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.011
You should also look at the company's Incurred Claim Ratio

00:05:25.011 --> 00:05:27.600
The formula for the Incurred Claim Ratio is

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.600
Total value of claim settled by an insurer

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.600
Divided by the total value of premium Collected by the

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.600
insurance company

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.117
And if we multiply this by 100 Then it comes out in

00:05:37.117 --> 00:05:39.600
percentage terms Now if a company's

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.000
ICR is less than 50%

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Then we can understand that the company

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.980
Is collecting a lot of premium

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.000
But is not settling the claims accordingly

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
So this is very good

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.980
According to the insurance company's business

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Because the company is profiting a lot

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.980
But when you are getting insurance from that company

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
Then this is a negative sign for us

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Because the company knows

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.000
That people look at the claim settlement ratio

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.980
That's why the company easily passes

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.000
The small claims

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.000
And the big claims

00:06:08.399 --> 00:06:10.379
Sometimes the company delays in passing the big claims

00:06:10.399 --> 00:06:12.399
Or rejects them

00:06:12.399 --> 00:06:14.399
Or partially passes them

00:06:14.399 --> 00:06:16.399
So that the claim settlement ratio is correct

00:06:16.399 --> 00:06:18.379
Let's understand this with an example

00:06:18.399 --> 00:06:22.399
